description=The apocalypse is a lousy dinner guest. Share a meal with another survivor nearby and both feel a little better. No plates or furniture required. <LINE> <LINE>
description=<H2> How to share a meal <LINE> <TEXT>
description=- Stay within four tiles, on the same floor, with clear sight. Open doors count. Walls, closed doors and windows do not. <LINE>
description=- Each person must finish at least five hunger points in one normal food action, within ten game minutes of the other person. Stay nearby. <LINE>
description=- Both get 5 less boredom and 3 less unhappiness, at most once per 24 game hours. A meal with good company! <LINE> <LINE>
description=<H2> Setup and limits <LINE> <TEXT>
description=No required mods. Install on the server and every client. Add DinnerTogether to the server Mods list. Tiny bites and interrupted actions do not count. Eating alone has no effect. <LINE> <LINE>
description=The server saves cooldowns across restarts. A replacement character on the same username or local slot keeps the cooldown. Network split-screen notifications target the first local player. Safe to add or remove. No new items or world objects. The illustration shows a mood, not a required table setup.
